WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.210
This cased daguerreotype,
now at the Amon Carter Museum in Fort Worth,

2
00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:08.810
is catalogued simply
as Native American, Plains Nations.

3
00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:14.210
It's usually dated around 1849
and attributed to Thomas Easterly,

4
00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:16.730
the photographer
who made Keokuk's portrait.

5
00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:18.830
Notice the stiff pose.

6
00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:23.330
Early exposures took many seconds,
so sitters had to hold still.

7
00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:26.900
Notice the gilt oval,
and the absence of any setting.

8
00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:28.870
And notice the title.

9
00:00:29.060 --> 00:00:33.730
It tells you what has been lost:
this man's name, and his nation.
